    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/739663",
      "sequence": 4,
      "source_sequence": 681,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Fueling Electrification: The Impact of Gas Prices on Hybrid Car Usage",
      "title_cn": "推动电气化：汽油价格对混合动力汽车使用的影响",
      "authors": [
        "Laura Grigolon",
        "Eunseong Park",
        "Kevin Remmy"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We use microlevel data on fuel consumption, mileage, and travel mode to study how plug-in hybrid drivers respond to fuel prices. When fuel prices rise, plug-in hybrids reduce fuel consumption more than gasoline and diesel cars. They do not proportionally reduce their mileage; instead, they increase electric charging. Since plug-in hybrids drive in electric mode for only half the distance suggested by official test cycle values, fuel prices are effective in improving the environmental performance of these vehicles.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们利用关于燃料消耗、行驶里程和出行方式的微观数据，研究插电式混合动力汽车驾驶员如何应对燃料价格。当燃料价格上涨时，插电式混合动力汽车比汽油和柴油汽车减少更多的燃料消耗。它们并未按比例减少行驶里程；相反，它们增加了电动充电。由于插电式混合动力汽车在电动模式下的行驶距离仅为官方测试循环值所建议的一半，燃料价格在改善这些车辆的环境性能方面是有效的。",
