    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/740146",
      "sequence": 8,
      "source_sequence": 831,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Downwind and Out: The Strategic Dispersion of Power Plants and Their Pollution",
      "title_cn": "顺风而下：电厂及其污染的战略性分散",
      "authors": [
        "John M. Morehouse",
        "Edward Rubin"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "In federalist systems, local governments may face incentives to export locally produced negative externalities. We empirically substantiate this externality-export strategy for air pollution using historical power-plant sitings, administrative borders, and prevailing wind directions. Using a simple, nonparametric test, we show that decision-makers disproportionately sited coal-fueled plants to reduce counties’/states’ downwind pollution exposure. Natural-gas-fueled plants—lower polluters—did not follow this strategy. We then illustrate the extreme exportability of coal plants’ pollution: within six hours, 50% of coal plants’ emissions leave their source states—and 99% depart source counties. These results highlight how local strategic responses challenge federalist systems.",
      "abstract_cn": "在联邦制体系中，地方政府可能面临激励，将本地产生的负外部性输出到外部。我们利用历史上的电厂选址、行政边界和盛行风向，实证证实了这种针对空气污染的外部性输出策略。通过一个简单的非参数检验，我们表明决策者不成比例地将燃煤电厂选址以减少县/州的下风向污染暴露。天然气电厂——污染较低——并未遵循这一策略。随后，我们展示了燃煤电厂污染的极端可输出性：在六小时内，燃煤电厂排放的50%离开其来源州——而99%离开来源县。这些结果凸显了地方战略反应如何挑战联邦制体系。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
